# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This org root is TWO things at once:
#   1. your working folder — your project repos, your mail, your dashboards
#   2. the source of one publishable toolkit — agentmail/
#
# Only (2) is tracked. This file is a WHITELIST, not a blocklist: everything at
# the root is ignored, and a handful of things are re-admitted by name. A
# blocklist would leak the first project folder someone forgets to list; this
# cannot. If a new file at the root is not showing up in `git status`, that is
# working as designed — add an explicit `!` line for it below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ignore everything at the root, including dotfiles
/*

# ── re-admit the toolkit and its front page ─────────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/agentmail/
!/.github/

# ── never tracked, and why ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# /<your projects>/     each project is its own git repo with its own remote.
#                       Nesting them here would either swallow their history
#                       or push someone else's code into this one.
#
# /.agent-mail/         the live mail spool. It holds the actual bodies of
#                       every message your agents have sent each other —
#                       plans, credentials-adjacent discussion, client names.
#                       A cloner does not need your mail; they need the shape,
#                       and `agentmail/bin/agentmail-init` builds that in one
#                       command. Shipping the spool would publish your
#                       network's private correspondence.
#
# /CLAUDE.md            your overseer's identity: your name, your machine, your
#                       absolute paths, your standing rules. The blank version
#                       ships as agentmail/templates/OVERSEER_CLAUDE.md.
#
# /runbooks/            generated dashboards and deploy notes. network.html is
#                       a rendering of your live network — seat names, message
#                       subjects, contributor emails, commit messages. It is
#                       regenerated in two seconds from source; it should never
#                       be a commit.
#
# /overseer-tasks.md    your task board: what you are actually working on.

# ── inside the toolkit, a few things are still generated ────────────────────
agentmail/**/__pycache__/
agentmail/**/*.pyc
agentmail/**/.DS_Store
.DS_Store
